{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399","id":"pg_74e54733d9805875a7114433e1657bb7","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhixiangluo-10xproductivity-setup-python-md-9a7da40bc798-4433e1657bb7.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_420418cd9fc4591593ed0ab7c65d72da"],"title":"ZhixiangLuo/10xProductivity/setup-python.md @ 9a7da40bc798","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1821159ea11e4e0b59af05346dfb84c37c2f7c038772322048bdd0a81470166c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The connection philosophy prioritizes zero-friction auth: supported API tokens first, then Agent Browser over existing sessions; OAuth requiring the user to create their own app or register credentials is explicitly rejected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88a1bd886750686b0b20c4df52c45a5556c140c89121d5076bf250fed9809725"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions follow a 'run before you write' rule — every snippet must be executed and seen to succeed — and new tool work starts in TENX_PRIVATE_DIR/personal/, never directly in tool_connections/, with promotion to the public repo only via staging/ and a PR after verification and scrubbing."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1821159ea11e4e0b59af05346dfb84c37c2f7c038772322048bdd0a81470166c","clm_88a1bd886750686b0b20c4df52c45a5556c140c89121d5076bf250fed9809725"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399","id":"pg_7869d573b11058d6953a3a5701b4d8b6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhixiangluo-10xproductivity-add-new-tool-md-9a7da40bc798-3a5701b4d8b6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c068935bbab55ca4b80f4ee5db280e47"],"title":"ZhixiangLuo/10xProductivity/add-new-tool.md @ 9a7da40bc798","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399","id":"pg_80118cd16e185c82826baca2ecfc3bf8","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhixiangluo-10xproductivity-legal-notice-md-9a7da40bc798-aca2ecfc3bf8.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_cdaafe084e1f5ef1a29786b12695b1c4"],"title":"ZhixiangLuo/10xProductivity/LEGAL_NOTICE.md @ 9a7da40bc798","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_03da786cb1e986324876eeb3e75a1dd024f28e3b5322f9305e90dd8f763f0eb1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture separates a push layer (triggers that detect events via desktop/browser notifications, sessions, email, or polling and wake workflows) from a pull layer (tool connections that fetch context or act), with a thin local runtime handling polling, scheduling, state, dedupe, replies, and agent invocation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_068019eb27bee991cf8ead377e1c05a04b8c701f520f710b23b4e3c881a0df57"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is positioned as a local-first personal AI assistant stack that reuses the user's existing coding agent, browser sessions, desktop apps, and permissions, explicitly avoiding new company-wide platforms, Slack apps, webhooks, or IT approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_15d4cdd5398ecc3101971110c8412b4c42ec86980f9a209a15a30b39a14a89ee"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup requires a coding agent (Cursor, Claude Code, or Codex), a Python virtualenv with an editable dev install (pip install -e \".[dev]\"), and optionally Python/Playwright setup per setup-python.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1f3451b5fef5a21d4077c8ce5bb84ca8f4ab660e2e6e36ff4d435370789cac88"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A second CLI, 10x-standup-prep, supports a --meeting-context flag and a --dry-run mode; posting to Slack requires reviewing output first and setting TENX_STANDUP_PREP_SLACK_CHANNEL before using --post."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69aa9a134f225fb648805cabe845156d4f62a23851e72d3f0c06e007e8af48b3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Packaged Cursor and Claude Code skills cover tool setup, enterprise search, workflow creation, UI surface discovery, colleague distillation, and an assistant inbox/orchestrator skill."},{"claim_ids":["clm_701d4f4cf6e92d869a0fbe8a1a44bb64694ab3eef424c4a71f9da30d32056670"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The runtime exposes a CLI entry point 10x-host that takes --trigger, --workflow, and --engine arguments, e.g. running a slack-polling trigger with the assistant workflow and the cursor engine."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88a1bd886750686b0b20c4df52c45a5556c140c89121d5076bf250fed9809725"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions follow a 'run before you write' rule — every snippet must be executed and seen to succeed — and new tool work starts in TENX_PRIVATE_DIR/personal/, never directly in tool_connections/, with promotion to the public repo only via staging/ and a PR after verification and scrubbing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88fb1340656cfebd26cee1886e7ced6d0ab09ee1500cbc411cd840262b348812"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the README's status table, tool connections, enterprise search, and agent skills are available today, while triggers, runtime, and reusable workflows are early; learning and memory (scheduled reflection, durable memory) are roadmap items not yet complete."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9950b4a60820e773f2ce4d51d2fabea10b1407ce6130d14c82b677d087cfff22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Private runtime state lives outside the repo by default under ~/.10xProductivity/ (.env tokens, personal/ recipes, verified_connections.md, tmp/ for trigger and scheduler state), overridable via the TENX_PRIVATE_DIR environment variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a0506b716647e182c956caf14563aa7d5fe90c48f15c39764eeca067066e6efd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README warns that some workflows automate actions on external platforms in ways that may violate platform Terms of Service, and directs users to LEGAL_NOTICE.md before running automation scripts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b1dbd2ca5dfce865a0c23e8472d8e1e88b70d723c388d6f9d7b6b936ccae5d8b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is organized into tool_connections/, triggers/, runtime/, workflows/, tests/, .cursor/skills/, .claude/skills/, and staging/, plus setup guides such as setup.md, add-new-tool.md, and setup-python.md."}],"claim_ids":["clm_03da786cb1e986324876eeb3e75a1dd024f28e3b5322f9305e90dd8f763f0eb1","clm_068019eb27bee991cf8ead377e1c05a04b8c701f520f710b23b4e3c881a0df57","clm_15d4cdd5398ecc3101971110c8412b4c42ec86980f9a209a15a30b39a14a89ee","clm_1f3451b5fef5a21d4077c8ce5bb84ca8f4ab660e2e6e36ff4d435370789cac88","clm_69aa9a134f225fb648805cabe845156d4f62a23851e72d3f0c06e007e8af48b3","clm_701d4f4cf6e92d869a0fbe8a1a44bb64694ab3eef424c4a71f9da30d32056670","clm_88a1bd886750686b0b20c4df52c45a5556c140c89121d5076bf250fed9809725","clm_88fb1340656cfebd26cee1886e7ced6d0ab09ee1500cbc411cd840262b348812","clm_9950b4a60820e773f2ce4d51d2fabea10b1407ce6130d14c82b677d087cfff22","clm_a0506b716647e182c956caf14563aa7d5fe90c48f15c39764eeca067066e6efd","clm_b1dbd2ca5dfce865a0c23e8472d8e1e88b70d723c388d6f9d7b6b936ccae5d8b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399","id":"pg_9874205e2b185911ae80b7d2b24739a7","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/zhixiangluo-10xproductivity-readme-md-9a7da40bc798-b7d2b24739a7.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8b423c7f8e1e5eb09bfee65848222ffc"],"title":"ZhixiangLuo/10xProductivity/README.md @ 9a7da40bc798","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:34:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a524d100cdee46bc9d0e6a70073be399"}
